    "text": "Let G ⩽ Sym(Ω) be a finite primitive permutation group with a regular\nsuborbit (that is, G has a trivial 2-point stabiliser). Then is it true that for all\nα, β ∈ Ω, there exists γ ∈ Ω such that the 2-point stabilisers Gα,γ and Gβ,γ are both\ntrivial?                                                     T. C. Burness, M. Giudici",
